'' '-mt' SETS __FB_MT__, and until 2026-09-07 it set nothing at all. The option was
'' parsed into a field nothing read: the define was hard-coded to 0 and the link
'' always named libfb.a, so '-mt' selected the single-threaded runtime in silence
'' while telling every header it was not threading.
''
'' THE VALUE IS fbc's AND WAS MEASURED, not assumed: '#print __FB_MT__' emits 0
'' without the flag and -1 with it. -1 is FreeBASIC's true, so '#if' selects on it.
''
'' IT IS DEFINED EITHER WAY. '#ifdef __FB_MT__' is true with or without the flag --
'' checked against fbc, which prints MT for both -- so code testing for threading
'' must use '#if'. That is the trap this file exists to pin: a test written with
'' '#ifdef' would pass whatever the option did.
''
'' The archive selection cannot be asserted here (the runner captures tiko's output,
'' not clang's argv) and is recorded in the commit: a directory holding only
'' libfbmt.a links under '-mt' and fails without it, and a two-thread program
'' returns the same count as fbc's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -mt --parse-only %s
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: TKO0309
'' EXPECT-OUT: threading is on

#if __FB_MT__
#error threading is on
#endif
print "unreachable"
